# D-169. Casting 4's 42fe57b added tests/test_survey.py::test_a_triple_quoted_string_
# hides_its_parens_from_the_join and took the suite from 148 defined tests to 149,
# leaving the README Status section stating a count nobody could reach and
# test_status_passing_count_matches_the_collected_suite red on assert 148 == 149. The
# first block shows all three places that number is written -- README.md:194 and the
# two prose copies in test_readme.py's FR-039 / AC-039 red-first record, at the
# pre-change commit b188ff0 and at HEAD -- so the re-pin is visible as a diff rather
# than asserted. The second counts the suite by the same AST rule _scan_module uses,
# per module, and the third is what pytest independently collects and reports: 149
# either way, with the single red being the GI-007 scope guard that names this run's
# own committed evidence/ logs and goes green on the lead's strip commit.
#
# The last block re-measures every other count the Status section states about this
# suite, because a stale number is rarely alone. Three held and are unchanged: eight
# modules against eight tests/test_*.py on disk; six of the seven scripts with one
# test module each, listed script by script, with rendered.py the one that has none;
# and test_harness.py measuring five things against its five tests in the table above.

